## AdSense, privacy, and legal launch checklist

Google's policies specifically prohibit artificial impressions/clicks, click encouragement, deceptive placement, ads that imitate site navigation, and certain placements that interfere with normal site behavior. Ad placements therefore need to be visually independent from RankNova's upload areas and primary actions. citeturn696138search0turn696138search1turn696138search2

Privacy should be implemented as an engineering property rather than only as a footer document. GDPR principles call for lawfulness/transparency, purpose limitation, data minimization, storage limitation, security, and accountability, including privacy by design/default. citeturn832256search0turn832256search1

For a US-facing service, CCPA obligations depend on whether the business falls within the law's coverage thresholds; covered businesses must support rights such as know, delete, correct, opt out of sale/sharing, and—in applicable circumstances—limits on sensitive-data use. citeturn832256search2turn832256search3

COPPA generally becomes relevant when a commercial service is directed to children under 13 and collects personal information, or where a general-audience service has actual knowledge that it is collecting such information from a child. RankNova therefore should not unnecessarily ask visitors for age or date of birth. citeturn832256search4turn832256search5

The DMCA process deserves special care. A US online service provider seeking applicable Section 512 safe-harbor protection may need to designate and register an agent, publish the agent's contact details, and respond appropriately to valid notices; simply placing “DMCA compliant” in the footer does not create that protection. citeturn817648search6turn817648search7

Before launch, prioritize the following:

1. **Real-tool acceptance:** QR PNG/SVG generation, genuine PDF compression, and genuine background removal must all pass real-input tests. Any unconfigured AI provider must produce a clear unavailable state, not a fabricated image.

2. **Upload security:** enforce allowlisted types, signature checks, resource limits, random temporary filenames, processing isolation, deletion and rate limiting. OWASP recommends layered validation because no single file-validation technique is sufficient. citeturn536294search9

3. **Admin lockdown:** use owner-only Firebase authorization, deny-by-default Firestore rules, server-side authorization, emulator tests and least-privilege IAM. citeturn696138search5turn696138search6

4. **Privacy-first defaults:** retain no user files by default, log no content, clearly disclose any server/API processing, and implement real deletion behavior consistent with the published policy. citeturn832256search0

5. **Legal review:** review Privacy Policy, Terms, Acceptable Use, copyright/DMCA procedure, AI-provider/model terms, applicable consumer privacy obligations and local cyber-law obligations with counsel appropriate to the operator's jurisdiction. Export-control requirements can also depend on the exact AI hardware/model/provider and end use; current BIS guidance shows that some advanced-computing/AI activities can trigger EAR restrictions, so avoid broad claims of universal export compliance. citeturn832256search8turn832256search7

6. **Consent:** deploy an appropriate consent system before enabling advertising/optional tracking in jurisdictions that require it; Google has specific certified-CMP requirements for its publisher products in the EEA, UK and Switzerland. citeturn817648search0turn817648search1

7. **Ad layout audit:** keep ads away from upload, Generate, Compress, Remove Background and Download controls; do not reward views, force pre-roll ad viewing, ask for clicks or artificially generate traffic. citeturn696138search0turn696138search1turn696138search2

8. **Content quality:** publish substantive homepage/tool explanations, FAQs, About, Contact and a small number of genuinely helpful articles. Google requires indexable public content for search eligibility, while AdSense prohibits pages created principally to display advertisements. citeturn817648search4turn696138search0

9. **SEO verification:** test rendered titles, descriptions, canonical URLs, crawlable links, 200/404 status handling, robots.txt and sitemap.xml before submitting the sitemap. citeturn817648search3turn817648search5

10. **Cost controls:** configure Cloud Run maximum instances, AI-provider quotas and Cloud Billing alerts. Google notes that ordinary budget alerts notify you but generally do not automatically stop usage. citeturn430749search4

