Google AI Studio's present deployment path maps naturally to this workflow because Build mode can produce full-stack apps, synchronize source through GitHub and publish to Cloud Run. Firebase supplies authentication/database infrastructure, while Firestore supports scheduled backups once the relevant billing plan is enabled. citeturn430749search0turn696138search3turn430749search1

The most important launch principle is simple: **RankNova should be useful even with every advertisement disabled.** The three tools should produce genuine outputs, public pages should contain original helpful content, uploaded files should be treated as untrusted and temporary, and advertising should be layered on only after the product itself is stable. That architecture aligns the business goal—organic utility traffic plus later AdSense monetization—with Google's publisher policies rather than making ads the core user experience. citeturn696138search0turn696138search1